WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.405
This is the N and C Gravity Sewer and Channel tool.

00:03.455 --> 00:07.199
It solves Manning's equation for a round pipe or an open

00:07.249 --> 00:10.248
channel, and it shows its work on every step.

00:10.648 --> 00:11.843
First, the banner.

00:11.893 --> 00:13.227
This tool is a beta.

00:13.277 --> 00:17.448
It is not for design use, and every result goes to a New York

00:17.498 --> 00:18.347
licensed P.E.

00:18.397 --> 00:19.108
for review.

00:19.508 --> 00:20.690
The rule is simple.

00:20.740 --> 00:24.322
Of flow, size, slope and depth, leave exactly one blank.

00:24.372 --> 00:25.943
The page solves that one.

00:25.993 --> 00:29.834
Here flow is blank, so an eight inch pipe at zero point four

00:29.884 --> 00:33.855
zero percent, half full, carries zero point three eight c f s.

00:34.255 --> 00:38.097
Manning's equation sits across the top with today's numbers in

00:38.147 --> 00:38.286
it.

00:38.336 --> 00:42.052
One point four eight six over n, times area, times hydraulic

00:42.102 --> 00:45.442
radius to the two thirds, times slope to the one half.

00:45.492 --> 00:47.702
The solved term is outlined in blue.

00:47.752 --> 00:49.774
A term that just changed flashes.

00:50.174 --> 00:53.618
To solve for something else, click solve for this beside it.

00:53.668 --> 00:56.065
Here we keep the flow and solve for slope.

00:56.115 --> 00:59.734
The answer shows right in the blank field, and the other fields

00:59.784 --> 01:00.782
keep their values.

01:01.182 --> 01:05.135
The drawing puts area, wetted perimeter and hydraulic radius on

01:05.185 --> 01:05.771
the shape.

01:05.821 --> 01:08.313
The orange line is the wetted perimeter.

01:08.363 --> 01:11.363
The purple bar is R, standing next to the depth.

01:11.413 --> 01:13.269
Hydraulic radius is not depth.

01:13.319 --> 01:16.701
In a half full pipe it is one quarter of the diameter.

01:17.101 --> 01:20.727
For a round pipe, the hydraulic elements chart shows where you

01:20.777 --> 01:20.964
are.

01:21.014 --> 01:22.861
Read across at your depth ratio.

01:22.911 --> 01:26.359
Each curve is the partial value divided by the flowing full

01:26.409 --> 01:26.715
value.

01:26.765 --> 01:29.324
Velocity peaks near eighty one percent full.

01:29.374 --> 01:32.051
Discharge peaks near ninety four percent full.

01:32.451 --> 01:36.002
Near the top, a pipe can carry the same flow at two depths.

01:36.052 --> 01:39.664
The page reports both and draws the second as a dashed line.

01:39.714 --> 01:41.434
Neither one is pressure flow.

01:41.834 --> 01:45.291
For round pipe, the Ten States twenty fourteen checks run on

01:45.341 --> 01:45.876
their own.

01:45.926 --> 01:49.325
Eight inches minimum, and two feet per second flowing full.

01:49.375 --> 01:53.007
That velocity check always uses n of zero point zero one three,

01:53.057 --> 01:54.937
even when you type a different n.

01:54.987 --> 01:56.924
A ditch does not fail these rules.

01:57.324 --> 01:59.564
Manning n is a material choice.

01:59.614 --> 02:02.593
Pick one from the list, or type your own.

02:02.643 --> 02:07.247
Anything smoother than zero point zero one zero gets a warning.

02:07.647 --> 02:08.971
Watch your slope units.

02:09.021 --> 02:12.676
Type zero point four with feet per foot selected, and the page

02:12.726 --> 02:15.065
warns you that is a forty percent grade.

02:15.115 --> 02:18.232
Switch to percent and the flow drops back to a tenth.

02:18.632 --> 02:22.021
For a ditch, pick rectangle, trapezoid or triangle.

02:22.071 --> 02:26.202
Width and depth are in feet, and the Ten States pipe rules are

02:26.252 --> 02:27.011
not applied.

02:27.411 --> 02:29.689
Open channels get a rating curve instead:

02:29.739 --> 02:33.096
depth against flow and velocity, with critical depth marked.

02:33.146 --> 02:36.446
Froude number and specific energy are shown for information

02:36.496 --> 02:36.730
only.

02:37.130 --> 02:40.400
Show the work lists every step with your numbers in it, so a

02:40.450 --> 02:42.502
reviewer can check the answer by hand.

02:43.130 --> 02:46.810
When you are done, copy the report, copy a link that reopens

02:46.860 --> 02:49.669
these exact inputs, or print the page for P.E.

02:49.719 --> 02:50.104
review.
